        {
          "id": "SP_MUCROPETRALIELLA_LOCULIFERA_HARMER_1957",
          "name": "Mucropetraliella loculifera Harmer, 1957",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Mucropetraliella",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Colony encrusting, multiserial, unilaminar. Autozooids distinct with shallow interzooidal furrows, large, polygonal, longer than wide (mean L / W = 1.30). Frontal shield convex, evenly perforated with large pseudopores set in polygonal depressions. Orifice seemingly bell-shaped with occlusor-laminae and median denticle; lateral denticles and condyles not observed; a pointed suboral mucro present. Two small oral spine bases visible in one of the zooids. Adventitious avicularia of different sizes and shapes present, small and oval (95 µm long by 75 µm wide) to large and teardrop-shaped (195 µm long by 125 µm wide), placed either below or lateral to the orifice, or elsewhere on the frontal shield. Ooecium not observed.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:1009847"
        },
